From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:03:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] notificationmanager: group notifications by conversation
Description:
 A chat with many messages filled every view, since notifications could
 only be grouped by application.
 .
 New hint x-kde-conversation-id (ConversationRole) and group mode
 GroupConversationsFlat: notifications of the same application and
 conversation form a group; without the hint the summary (the sender of
 a message) stands for the conversation, the jobs of an application stay
 together. When a view may only show the application, summary and
 conversation are empty and the notifications group by application.
 .
 The grouping model now follows its source when a notification is
 replaced with one that belongs to another group, and when the rows of
 the source change within a layout change; it kept stale rows before.
 Rebuilding the groups within a model reset no longer announces removed
 rows (views and proxy models crashed on them). The visibility model
 reports a changed visibility as a filter change and a change of the
 content instead of a layout change. Switching between the grouping modes
 and back from no grouping keeps the proxy chain connected.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
---
